# Signatures in src/tweaks that are KNOWN to match more than once, and are used anyway.
#
#   <name>   <hits>   # why this is safe
#
# A signature matching twice normally means "lengthen it": it still resolves, to whichever match the
# scanner reached first, and that is a coin flip nobody documented. These are the exceptions, where
# the ambiguity was measured and the first match is the wanted one.
#
# ORDER-DEPENDENT BY CONSTRUCTION. Every entry here is a bet that the twins keep their current
# relative order in the binary. That is exactly the kind of thing a game update can flip without
# changing a single byte of either function, and nothing would look wrong -- the mod would call the
# other twin and misbehave in a way no log line explains. So after ANY game update, re-verify every
# entry here by hand (pdbsym.py addr <rva> on each match) before trusting a green run.

SIG_ADDFORCE  2   # FBodyInstance::AddForce and ::AddTorqueInRadians have byte-identical prologues
                  # -- same shape, same four arguments, 0x4f bytes each. Verified against the Epic
                  # PDB 2026-09-01: first match 0x2e47b50 = AddForce, second 0x2e47e40 =
                  # AddTorqueInRadians. body_feel.cpp takes the first, which is the right one.

SIG_WIDGET_SET_OPACITY  2   # UWidget::SetRenderOpacity and UE::MovieScene::SetRenderOpacity(UObject*,
                  # float) are the same bytes for their whole 0x79 length and have the same effect
                  # and the same (object, float) arguments -- the free function is the member inlined.
                  # Verified against the Epic PDB 2026-09-18: 0x27bb390 = the MovieScene one, 0x27bb410 =
                  # the member. ORDER DOES NOT MATTER HERE: either match is the right call.

SIG_SET_PHYS_VELOCITY  2   # UPrimitiveComponent::SetPhysicsAngularVelocityInRadians and ::SetPhysicsLinearVelocity
                  # are the same bytes for their whole 0x42 length (they differ only in the FBodyInstance call
                  # they forward to, which is a wildcarded rel32). BOTH ARE WANTED: sit.cpp takes the first as
                  # the angular one and the second (TwkScanExeNth 1) as the linear one. Verified against the
                  # Epic PDB 2026-09-18: 0x2ed85a0 = angular, 0x2ed85f0 = linear; Steam 0x2e9b080 / 0x2e9b0d0,
                  # the same order and the same 0x50 apart. ORDER MATTERS: flipped, a thrown board spins madly
                  # and goes nowhere (same arguments, so nothing crashes). Re-verify after any update.
